WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.920
Whether it's the devilish new characters,&nbsp;
cryptic answers to ancient prophecies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.960
or giant worms, the trailer for Dune: Part Two&nbsp;
is full of details that you might've missed.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.940
It can be argued that the parent-child&nbsp;
relationship between Lady Jessica and Paul may be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:19.860
one of the most dynamic in science-fiction. Dune&nbsp;
author Frank Herbert's characterization of Lady&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:25.320
Jessica is nuanced, with her motives to conceive&nbsp;
Paul being her desperate love of Duke Leto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.780
Atreides and her personal desire to bring about&nbsp;
the Kwisatz Haderach — the universe's super being.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:36.240
But as close as she and Paul are in the first&nbsp;
film, the cracks begin to show when Paul realizes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:41.520
how his Bene Gesserit lineage has affected him.&nbsp;
He still has a long way to go before achieving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:46.200
his destiny, but the closer he gets, the more it&nbsp;
pushes him away from those who can understand him.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.500
Though Paul seems to believe that he&nbsp;
must cling to his father's principles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.240
he's already slipping. His visions have shown&nbsp;
him that he will start a intergalactic holy war,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.800
and with Duke Leto not believing in revenge,&nbsp;
it's fair to say he wouldn't approve of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.060
genocide that Paul is seemingly destined&nbsp;
to cause. This brings Paul inner turmoil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:07.020
as he doesn't want to be capable of these&nbsp;
unspeakable acts — but Jessica continues&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:10.267
to push him, all while he starts&nbsp;
pulling away from her influence.

00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:12.014
"We gave them something to hope for."

00:01:12.014 --> 00:01:13.029
"That's not hope!"

00:01:13.029 --> 00:01:17.160
In the Dune: Part Two trailer, we see Lady&nbsp;
Jessica gasping for air and opening her eyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:21.660
now the vibrant blue of the Fremen. This&nbsp;
color change usually indicates prolonged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:26.640
exposure to Spice — an addictive psychoactive&nbsp;
substance found only on the planet Arrakis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.000
considered the most valuable&nbsp;
substance in the universe. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.080
the blood crusting Jessica's nose hints at&nbsp;
a very specific source for her blue eyes.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:39.420
It's likely that this scene is part of a "spice&nbsp;
agony" — a ritual in which members of the Bene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:44.400
Gesserit voluntarily ingest a poison known&nbsp;
as the Water of Life — liquid harvested from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:48.900
sandworms that die from drowning. Although the&nbsp;
Water of Life is fatal even in small quantities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:52.980
high-ranking members of the sisterhood&nbsp;
are able to transform the substance into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:57.960
a benign liquid with their mental powers. This&nbsp;
incredibly painful transformation unlocks a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:02.040
level of power within those who survive,&nbsp;
transforming them into a Reverend Mother.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:06.240
There's even a possible glimpse of the Water&nbsp;
of Life a few seconds earlier in the trailer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:11.220
held in a glass vial by a cloaked figure.&nbsp;
Jessica's spice agony will probably play&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:16.020
a major part in her story throughout Dune: Part&nbsp;
Two, and this is most likely our first glimpse.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:20.460
Princess Irulan is the eldest daughter&nbsp;
of the emperor of the known universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:24.660
But more importantly, anyone familiar&nbsp;
with the Dune saga will also be familiar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:28.140
with Irulan's work as a historian,&nbsp;
with Herbert beginning a significant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:31.500
number of chapters with an epigraph&nbsp;
from Irulan's professional writings.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:35.760
Typically, the passage will frame a notable&nbsp;
historical event as it officially happened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:40.800
and then the subsequent chapter will depict that&nbsp;
same event as it actually happened. In this way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:45.540
Irulan remains a consistent, prevalent force&nbsp;
in Dune without really being present for all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:49.380
the events of the story, not even physically&nbsp;
appearing in the first book until the end.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:53.340
While the Warner Bros. film mirrors this by&nbsp;
having Florence Pugh's princess making her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:57.240
debut in Dune Part Two, it also seems&nbsp;
that her role has been expanded upon.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:01.980
The Irulan in the first book did as she was&nbsp;
told and nothing more — a passive participant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:06.780
in her own life — though what she does later in&nbsp;
the series is another story entirely. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:10.800
the movie version of Irulan seems to be&nbsp;
actively asking questions and seeking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:15.000
answers. We can guess that director Denis&nbsp;
Villeneuve is planning to tie Irulan more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:19.440
closely into the main plot, or he might&nbsp;
be setting her up for future story arcs.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.780
Either way, it's safe to say&nbsp;
that no one in their right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:25.437
mind would cast Pugh in this part&nbsp;
and not let her explore the space.

00:03:25.437 --> 00:03:29.400
The longest section of the Dune: Part&nbsp;
Two trailer teases Paul's first ride on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:33.120
a sandworm. He places a thumper&nbsp;
in the sand and readies for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:36.840
massive creature's arrival. Over the&nbsp;
montage, we can hear Zendaya's Chani:

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.700
"Have you ever had a dream about your first ride?"

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:42.480
This question is likely more somber&nbsp;
than it initially seems. In the novel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:47.040
by the time Paul experiences his first sandworm&nbsp;
ride, he's had many visions of the future,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:51.480
and they're not all hopeful. In this scene,&nbsp;
Chani is asking if he's foreseen how his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:56.160
first ride will go, and whether or not he will&nbsp;
survive. Paul is a bit nervous to ride the worm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:00.660
and he knows that he's much older than most&nbsp;
Fremen when they do so for the first time. Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:03.720
the continued trailer dialogue&nbsp;
by Javier Bardem's Stilgar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:08.880
advising Paul how to ride Shai-Hulud, is also&nbsp;
pulled — nearly word for word — out of the book.

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:14.580
The Dune: Part Two trailer shows us Feyd-Rautha&nbsp;
Harkonnen — played by Austin Butler — in all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:18.840
his bald, treacherous glory. The great&nbsp;
foil to Paul Atreides in the Dune novel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:21.840
Feyd is the nephew and intended successor of Baron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:25.740
Vladimir Harkonnen — played on screen&nbsp;
in Dune: Part One by Stellan Skarsgård.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:30.420
Feyd bears the same drab, reptilian look as&nbsp;
the rest of his vicious family, with most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:34.800
of his moments in the trailer shot in complete&nbsp;
black-and-white. We see him participating in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:40.200
gladiatorial arenas on Giedi Prime — the Harkonnen&nbsp;
homeworld glimpsed briefly in the first film. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:45.300
also see an interaction with the Bene Gesserit,&nbsp;
Lady Margot Fenring — played by Léa Seydoux.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:49.320
Finally, we see what appears to be a&nbsp;
shot of Feyd facing off against Paul,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:51.780
with Paul uttering the famous Fremen challenge,

00:04:51.935 --> 00:04:54.600
"May thy knife chip and shatter."

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:57.300
We won't spoil it here, but if&nbsp;
you've already read the book,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.460
you know exactly what this moment leads to.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:03.960
The trailer gives audience members their&nbsp;
very first glimpse at Lady Margot. Though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:07.620
she becomes a major character later in&nbsp;
the Dune book series, it seems her part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:11.100
in Villeneuve's film may have been expanded&nbsp;
from her original role in the first novel.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:15.900
Margot is a member of the Bene Gesserit — the&nbsp;
powerful matriarchal order who are partially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:21.240
responsible for the destruction of House Atreides&nbsp;
on Arrakis. They've spent centuries orchestrating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:26.460
a selective breeding program to cross bloodlines&nbsp;
of the universe's noble houses, and hope to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:31.080
mate Margot with Feyd-Rautha Harkonnen. This&nbsp;
will give the secret organization a leg up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:34.020
as they'll have a member of House&nbsp;
Harkonnen fully in their control,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:36.540
doubling the amount of power in their possession.

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:40.260
Book fans know that Margot's fate&nbsp;
and Paul's are closely intertwined,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:45.060
and that ultimately Paul's rise will precipitate&nbsp;
Margot's fall. But, of course, this adaptation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:49.320
of Dune might switch things around a bit. For&nbsp;
now, it's clear that Margot is here to stay.

00:05:49.646 --> 00:05:54.180
House Harkonnen has been a shadow on House&nbsp;
Atreides from the opening moments of Dune:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:59.280
Part One, but if you thought the Baron was bad,&nbsp;
just wait for Feyd. Villeneuve told Vanity Fair,

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:03.120
"Austin Butler brought to the screen something&nbsp;
that would be a cross between a psychotic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:05.760
sociopath serial killer and Mick Jagger."

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:09.180
This features briefly in the&nbsp;
trailer as Feyd duels in an arena,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:13.800
observed by Lady Margot. As we've said, the&nbsp;
connection between the noble psychopath and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:18.540
the Bene Gesserit is significant. Established&nbsp;
in the first film, the Bene Gesserit are intent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:22.980
on bringing about the Kwisatz Haderach&nbsp;
through centuries of meticulous breeding.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:25.680
"You were told to bear only daughters. But you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:28.470
and your pride, thought you could&nbsp;
produce the Kwisatz Haderach."

00:06:28.692 --> 00:06:32.400
Had Jessica given birth to a girl, as was&nbsp;
originally planned, the child would have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:36.900
eventually wed Feyd in a political marriage,&nbsp;
with their offspring likely being the Kwisatz&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:42.300
Haderach. Now Paul is rising as the messiah of&nbsp;
Arrakis, cutting out the Harkonnens completely.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:46.413
But the Bene Gesserit don't appear to be&nbsp;
giving up on the Harkonnens quite yet.

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:50.640
The planet of Arrakis is foreboding and&nbsp;
hostile, even for those who possess the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:54.960
technology to travel among the stars. The&nbsp;
desert planet requires specialized skills&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:59.400
and knowledge for someone to be able to survive.&nbsp;
Although the planetary colonists of ruling noble&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:04.620
houses struggle to cultivate Spice, the Fremen —&nbsp;
Arrakis' indigenous population — are well adapted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:08.534
utilizing several novel technologies&nbsp;
that allow their people to flourish.

00:07:08.675 --> 00:07:10.775
"Thank you for the stillsuits."

00:07:10.775 --> 00:07:13.560
"They are of Fremen make. The best."

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:18.240
Among their most notable items are Maker Hooks&nbsp;
— featured prominently throughout the Dune:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:22.860
Part Two trailer. These hooks allow the&nbsp;
Fremen to mount and steer the giant sandworms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:26.160
and even though Paul is told not to&nbsp;
show off during his first ride attempt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:30.840
he's clearly quite good at it. Maker Hooks are&nbsp;
important within Fremen culture because riding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:36.060
a sandworm is a rite of passage into adulthood.&nbsp;
Fremen are able to use Maker Hooks to steer a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:40.740
sandworm by hooking into gaps in the sandworm's&nbsp;
plating, forcing the creatures to instinctively&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:44.580
move in the opposite direction. Even though&nbsp;
it looks like Paul is having fun in the Dune:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:48.960
Part Two trailer, this action means much more&nbsp;
than possessing a skill in the eyes of the Fremen.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:53.820
Dune: Part Two will feature many characters&nbsp;
on the hunt for Paul Atreides. As Princess&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:56.940
Irulan's voiceover questions his&nbsp;
fate after the Harkonnen attack,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.940 --> 00:08:01.980
we get a glimpse of Josh Brolin's Gurney Halleck&nbsp;
looking through a pair of binoculars. The editors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:06.060
have snuck in some clever imagery here,&nbsp;
since much of Gurney's story in the sequel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:09.960
will revolve around finding Paul and getting&nbsp;
revenge on someone he thought he could trust.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:15.300
Even before the Harkonnen attack, Duke Leto knew&nbsp;
there was a traitor embedded in House Atreides.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:20.520
In the novel, he even momentarily believed Jessica&nbsp;
could be the culprit — given her status as a Bene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:25.980
Gesserit — and Gurney is likewise suspicious.&nbsp;
Although audiences know Chang Chen's Dr. Yueh&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:30.300
was the traitor, Gurney hasn't learned that&nbsp;
information, and has continued to believe that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:34.920
Lady Jessica aided the Harkonnens. When we pick&nbsp;
up with him in Dune: Part Two, he's one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:39.660
few survivors of the original attack, searching&nbsp;
Arrakis for Paul, and vowing revenge on Jessica.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:42.240
While Gurney didn't have much to do in Dune:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:46.188
Part One, he still plays a significant&nbsp;
role as one of Paul's major allies.

00:08:46.188 --> 00:08:51.360
Once the door to Paul's potential opens, it cannot&nbsp;
be closed. His visions start simply at first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:56.520
with nightly dreams of Chani, whom he has yet to&nbsp;
meet. But more and more, his mind opens thanks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.520 --> 00:09:01.860
to the Spice, and soon he knows many things that&nbsp;
he wishes he didn't. As his destiny is revealed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:06.360
so is his mother's fate. Before Jessica&nbsp;
even confirms that she's pregnant in Dune:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:09.720
Part One, Paul tells her of the&nbsp;
baby she will have. In his mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:13.920
he sees Jessica's blue-within-blue eyes&nbsp;
and her future facial tattoos. Though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:18.960
we can't definitively say what the tattoos mean,&nbsp;
we can give a pretty accurate guess. Jessica&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:23.640
has built her life around the Bene Gesserit and&nbsp;
fulfilling the prophecy of the Kwisatz Haderach.

00:09:23.955 --> 00:09:31.455
"A mind — powerful enough&nbsp;
to bridge space and time."

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:33.240
Villeneuve told Vanity Fair,

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:37.260
"Lady Jessica is one of the masterminds&nbsp;
of Dune. She's trying to play her own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:40.200
agenda. The meaning of that look&nbsp;
would be unveiled in Part Two."

00:09:40.601 --> 00:09:45.401
It seems just as Paul comes to terms with his&nbsp;
place in the universe, so too does Jessica.

00:09:45.821 --> 00:09:49.800
There are many mysterious forces in play&nbsp;
throughout the galaxy depicted in Dune.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:54.000
Paul is the product of a long line of genetic&nbsp;
manipulation for the express purpose of creating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:59.880
a superhuman capable of leading humanity into a&nbsp;
universal golden age. This Bene Gesserit breeding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:04.380
program cultivates each successive generation to&nbsp;
possess greater acumen with their mental powers.

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:07.920
One of the most notable powers&nbsp;
is known as "The Voice." This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:10.260
skill is prominently seen — and heard — in Dune:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:14.600
Part One when Jessica and Paul escape their&nbsp;
assassination attempt during the Harkonnen coup.

00:10:14.738 --> 00:10:17.298
"Remove her gag."

00:10:19.456 --> 00:10:24.240
The power essentially allows its practitioners&nbsp;
to mentally dominate most individuals. In the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:28.080
final moments of the Dune: Part Two trailer,&nbsp;
Paul is addressing an assembly of Fremen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:33.236
Although the music swells, one can hear some&nbsp;
hint of The Voice's distinct auditory cue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.236 --> 00:10:37.076
maybe implying that Paul uses The&nbsp;
Voice to rally the Fremen to his cause.

